Carried patch, applied to the niri package until the channel ships it.

Upstream: niri commit 4adbf0039308cd0667f33e60e09ae480eca64056
https://github.com/YaLTeR/niri/commit/4adbf0039308cd0667f33e60e09ae480eca64056
"niri-session: import login environment without the deprecated systemd call"

Why: niri-session called `systemctl --user import-environment` with no
variable list, which systemd 260 answers with the warning "Calling
import-environment without a list of variable names is deprecated." The
session script runs with its stdout on the login VT, so the warning
prints on screen during login.

The patch swaps that call for `dbus-update-activation-environment
--systemd --all`, which imports the same environment into the systemd
user manager and into D-Bus, and keeps the old call only as a fallback
for systems without the dbus tools.

Drop this file when the channel's niri is newer than 26.04: the fix is
on niri's main branch and lands in the next release, and the patch then
fails to apply, which is the signal to remove it.

diff --git a/resources/niri-session b/resources/niri-session
index a9a4d94..40296ab 100755
--- a/resources/niri-session
+++ b/resources/niri-session
@@ -33,14 +33,29 @@ if hash systemctl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
     systemctl --user reset-failed
 
     # Import the login manager environment.
-    systemctl --user import-environment
-
-    # DBus activation environment is independent from systemd. While most of
-    # dbus-activated services are already using `SystemdService` directive, some
-    # still don't and thus we should set the dbus environment with a separate
-    # command.
+    #
+    # We intentionally import *all* environment variables.
+    # It's unfortunately commonplace for distros to initialize
+    # things with shell scripts and set environment variables.
+    #
+    # For example, debuginfod is initialized this way, and sets the
+    # $DEBUGINFOD_URLS environment variable. If we don't export it,
+    # then programs started from a systemd service (e.g. from xdg-autostart)
+    # will be unable to use debuginfod.
+    #
+    # We cannot possibly know and list all variables like this, so
+    # we import all of them into the environment. This also covers
+    # any variables the user may have customized, such as $PATH.
     if hash dbus-update-activation-environment 2>/dev/null; then
-        dbus-update-activation-environment --all
+        # The `--systemd` flag also sets the variables for systemd user services,
+        # so we don't need a separate `systemctl --user import-environment` call.
+        #
+        # (This also avoids the deprecation warning printed by
+        # a blanket `systemctl --user import-environment` that
+        # some people find very annoying.)
+        dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd --all
+    else
+        systemctl --user import-environment
     fi
 
     # Start niri and wait for it to terminate.
